3 TOP 5 DEEP DIVES

#1 Agentic Router: this is the cleanest new JEV-like mechanism because
proposal and selection adapt separately. It explicitly predicts
consequences before selecting an action, then grounds the selection
model in execution feedback. 6m: useful niche controller; 18m: likely
pattern for expensive/high-effect actions; 36m: bounded decision heads
may sit between generative planners and effectors. Privately
implication: QP can become a hard constraint/utility feature for the
selector. Smallest experiment: 20 safe shell/network-simulation tasks,
compare direct LLM action vs N candidates + consequence head + QP
veto. Falsifier: no gain in execution success/risk at matched cost.

#2 WasiAI A2A Gateway: unusually close to MONID because discovery,
orchestration and payment are one object. The key design is
quote-before-charge plus price-capped plan execution. Privately
implication: authority receipts should bind not only tool identity but
quoted plan, spend ceiling, selected providers and downstream
capability graph. Smallest experiment: shadow-plan three dummy agents
and verify that any provider substitution invalidates approval.
Falsifier: gateway cannot expose stable provider/capability identities
through orchestration.

#3 WorldAgen: important JEV adjacency because the controller is not
the world model. Shared representation feeds a policy head while
deployment experience updates world prediction. Privately implication:
let rich generative/world models adapt, but keep effect selection
bounded and separately auditable. Smallest experiment: extract
architecture concept into toy gridworld with mutable dynamics.
Falsifier: direct generative action selection remains better at equal
latency/sample budget.

#4 claude-remotion-skill: best new media primitive because output is
deterministic code and visual verification is mandatory. It gives the
media RSI loop an inspectable intervention surface. Smallest
experiment: create 5 variants from one script, extract identical frame
checkpoints, score with VLM, repair once, then compare human/YouTube
metrics. Falsifier: inspection-driven repair does not improve
measurable defects or retention proxies.

#5 mcpward: very small but strategically clean. Treat tool definitions
as external dependency contracts and make drift a CI failure rather
than a runtime surprise. Privately implication: capability
fingerprints belong in version control and deployment gates, not only
session state. Smallest experiment: snapshot 3 MCPs, mutate only
description/schema, ensure CI emits machine-readable delta and QP
selectively invalidates dependent grants. Falsifier: snapshots are too
unstable/noisy for real MCP releases.

